# Ladder step 3 (owner's order: UFS read-only). UFS has been in every ladder kernel since step 0 (the root is ios_system);
# this step adds no driver. It is the union of the two proven branches 1b (RTC CLKMON WDT HALT, port-2) and 2 (BUTTONS
# TOUCH, port-3) on the new common base hk-base-5, and its boot confirms the root stays read-only: the UFS block device has
# no write entry (d_write = eno_rdwrt, FWRITE opens -> EROFS) and its only write path, the persist store on ios_data, is
# silent without blazer_persist= (not on the line). Gates: the step-1b and step-2 lines together. (step2.config is not
# included: its minimal.config "not set" lines would turn 1b's drivers back off.)
#include step1b.config
CONFIG_HAKIOS_BUTTONS=y
CONFIG_HAKIOS_TOUCH=y
